  "articleBody": "Hiring a professional for grout work protects your tile installation from moisture and premature deterioration. When you compare contractors across the Denver metro area, focus on the details that determine long-term durability. \n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide\nFirst, ask which grout product fits your tile type and joint width, as unsuited mixtures can scratch delicate stone or slump in wide gaps. Second, confirm whether old, damaged grout will be fully removed before new product is applied, since tiling over cracked joints invites water underneath. Third, discuss their cure and sealing schedule. Proper sealing requires manufacturers' cure times before applying protective coats. Finally, check if their quote covers hidden moisture repairs if loose tiles appear during prep.\n\nProcess Clarity\nA solid contractor handles joint clearing, thorough cleaning, float application, meticulous haze removal, and correct sealant application once cured.\n\nIf you are planning a bathroom update or tile restoration, reach out to Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866 to discuss your tile project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}